cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use variant-workbench, please cite it as below, and also cite the
  data sources it is built from (see CITATIONS.md and NOTICE.md).
title: variant-workbench
type: software
authors:
  - alias: netmaster296
abstract: >-
  Open-source genetic variant database: a GRCh38 warehouse of genes, studied
  variants and their evidence from gnomAD, ClinVar, GENCODE, GTEx, the GWAS
  Catalog and MaveDB. Research use only.
repository-code: "https://github.com/netmaster296/variant-workbench"
url: "https://github.com/netmaster296/variant-workbench"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - genomics
  - bioinformatics
  - GRCh38
  - variants
  - ClinVar
  - GWAS
  - GTEx
  - MaveDB
  - open data
references:
  - type: article
    title: gnomAD flagship paper (gnomAD v4.1 data)
    authors:
      - family-names: Chen
        given-names: S.
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-023-06045-0
    notes: >-
      Confirmed on the gnomAD citation page, which gives the DOI and
      "(Chen et al., 2023)" but not the title.
  - type: article
    title: "GENCODE 2025: reference gene annotation for human and mouse"
    authors:
      - family-names: Mudge
        given-names: J. M.
    journal: Nucleic Acids Research
    year: 2025
    volume: 53
    issue: D1
    start: D966
    end: D975
    doi: 10.1093/nar/gkae1078
    notes: Confirmed on the GENCODE publications page.
  - type: article
    title: NHGRI-EBI GWAS Catalog (2025 Nucleic Acids Research update)
    authors:
      - family-names: Cerezo
        given-names: M.
    journal: Nucleic Acids Research
    year: 2025
    volume: 53
    issue: D1
    start: D998
    end: D1005
    doi: 10.1093/nar/gkae1070
    notes: >-
      Confirmed on the GWAS Catalog citation page, which lists authors,
      journal and DOI but not the title.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      MaveDB 2024: a curated community database with over seven million
      variant effects from multiplexed functional assays
    authors:
      - family-names: Rubin
        given-names: A. F.
    journal: Genome Biology
    year: 2025
    volume: 26
    issue: 1
    start: 13
    doi: 10.1186/s13059-025-03476-y
    notes: Confirmed on the MaveDB citation page.
  - type: data
    title: MaveDB bulk data dump mavedb-dump.2026062418131 (as of 2026-06-24)
    authors:
      - name: MaveDB
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20840937
    notes: Zenodo record 20840937. Licence CC0 1.0.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Saturation mutagenesis of twenty disease-associated regulatory elements
      at single base-pair resolution
    authors:
      - family-names: Kircher
        given-names: Martin
    journal: Nature Communications
    year: 2019
    doi: 10.1038/s41467-019-11526-w
    notes: >-
      PMID 31395865. Requested by the Fort Lauderdale notice on 28 MaveDB
      score sets (urn:mavedb:00000014 to 00000034); details from MaveDB main.json.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      A comprehensive map of missense trafficking variants in rhodopsin and
      their response to pharmacologic correction
    authors:
      - family-names: Manian
        given-names: Kannan V.
    year: 2025
    doi: 10.1101/2025.02.27.640335
    notes: >-
      bioRxiv preprint. Requested by MaveDB score set urn:mavedb:00001275-a-1
      together with dataset DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19558926; details from MaveDB
      main.json.
  - type: data
    title: RHO surface trafficking DMS scores (MaveDB urn:mavedb:00001275-a-1)
    authors:
      - family-names: Manian
        given-names: Kannan V.
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19558926
  - type: article
    title: GTEx v8 consortium paper
    authors:
      - name: GTEx Consortium
    journal: Science
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.1126/science.aaz1776
    notes: >-
      Not confirmed on an official GTEx page (seen only on a secondary page).
      GTEx also asks for its acknowledgement statement; see NOTICE.md.
  - type: article
    title: ClinVar (Landrum et al., Nucleic Acids Research 2016)
    authors:
      - family-names: Landrum
        given-names: M. J.
    journal: Nucleic Acids Research
    year: 2016
    doi: 10.1093/nar/gkv1222
    notes: >-
      Not confirmed: the ClinVar citation pages could not be read during the
      audit, and NCBI's preferred ClinVar citation was not seen. The 2014 paper
      is doi 10.1093/nar/gkt1113.
